WEBVTT

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.950
Kumiko...

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.450
There you are.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.030
Starting at noon, we have ensemble practice.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.990
Sorry, I'll be right there.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.850
Kumiko!

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.480
Kumiko-chan!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.340
What are you doing?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.130
Over here.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.060
We're taking a souvenir photo.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.900
Okay, strike a pose.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.580
Taki-sensei...

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.580
What are you doing here?

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.330
This way.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.000
Kumiko...

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.260
Reina.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.020
Can someone hold the certificate?

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.380
I'll pass.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.930
Asuka-senpai, could you duck a little?

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.550
Are you okay?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.990
All right, let's do a cheering pose.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.560
A cheering pose?

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.780
We've gotta express our joy 
with our whole bodies.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.330
I mean I'm happy, but...

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:43.740
<i>But...</i>

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.330
<i>I still can't believe it.</i>

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.710
<i>It isn't sinking in.</i>

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.450
Okay, here we go.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:52.090
Look this way.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.830
Strike a pose.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.460
Joy, huh?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:09.010
<i>Kitauji High School placed first at the 
Kyoto Concert Band Competition.</i>

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.450
<i>That isn't all.</i>

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.790
<i>We were chosen to represent Kyoto 
at the Kansai Competition.</i>

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.520
<i>Episode 1 
Mid-summer Fanfare</i>

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.200
Okay, everyone! Gather here!

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.190
Please.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:32.580
Um...

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:37.210
This is my first time doing this, so I 
don't really know what to say.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.050
Congratulations, everyone.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:44.060
No, we're the ones who 
should be thanking you.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.850
Guys, ready, and...

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.310
Thank you very much.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.770
Right.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.270
Thank you.

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.450
That's it?

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:59.230
What a buzzkill.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.950
As of today, we are representatives.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:10.240
In order to live up to that name, we must 
polish our performances even more.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:14.010
I would like you to prepare 
yourselves, here and now.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:15.290
Yes.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.230
Okay.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.920
Let's move.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.240
Thank you.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:53.650
They say school concert band performances

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:56.790
depend heavily on who the teacher is.

00:05:57.280 --> 00:05:59.750
I never thought we'd make it 
to the Kansai Competition.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.020
Thank you, as well, Matsumoto-sensei.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.460
Thank you.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.520
Ever since I was transferred here,

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:11.930
and ever since I first heard their performance,
I knew we had potential.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:18.440
Nakaseko-san and Tanaka-san have 
the talent to rival the top schools.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.310
Add to that, Kousaka-san and 
Kawashima-san took part.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.490
With people in the group 
to set good examples,

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.540
it's up to each individual 
to take responsibility.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.280
So, you believe they had room to grow.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.560
Of course.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.080
Though, there's a lot of work left to do.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.110
Um...

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.640
What is it, you two?

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.870
May we ask for a favor?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:42.010
Or some advice, rather?

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.210
Here.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.170
Have you each received the sheet?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:53.140
<b>Practice Schedule 
Morning: Individual Practice 
Afternoon: Ensemble Practice</b>

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.140
<i>You are expected to practice, 
even if it doesn't say anything.</i>

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:56.010
<i>The blanks on the schedule were a sign</i>

00:06:56.010 --> 00:07:00.780
<i>that going forward, our lives would 
be nothing like over summer break.</i>

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:06.230
August 17, 18, 19... For those three days,

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.700
we will be renting a nearby 
facility for a training camp.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.850
Please inform your parents 
when you get home today.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:18.080
Why does it say we have the 
15th and 16th before it off?

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.120
It's exactly what it says.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:21.950
We're taking a break?

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.690
I'd love to practice, but apparently,

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:30.970
the school mandates we take those days off.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.610
Can't we practice on our own?

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.930
They're closing down the school.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:37.120
Let's practice outside.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:37.770
Okay.

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.600
<i>Everyone was really banking 
on the competition.</i>

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:45.420
<i>The fact that we'd made the Kansai 
Regionals made the dream</i>

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:47.820
<i>of the Nationals into a potential reality.</i>

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:51.450
Anyway, we don't have much time left.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:55.160
Let's not squander this opportunity. 
For the third-years, of course,

00:07:55.160 --> 00:08:00.590
but even if you're a second- or 
first-year with more years ahead.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.500
Yes.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:06.150
Now, let's begin rehearsal.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.460
But first...

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:18.930
So, everyone, congratulations on making 
it into the Kansai Competition.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:21.260
We, Team Monaka,

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:25.270
would like to cheer for our club 
before the Kansai Competition,

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.730
as we always have.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.970
We'll perform with plenty of congratulatory 
spirit, so please hear us.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:34.700
All right.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.860
Here we go.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.400
Congratulations.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:14.490
Man, they've gotten good.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:30.770
Come on, President, why are you crying?

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.130
Sorry.

00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:34.970
Thank you very much.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.240
You must have all been so busy.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:44.100
Jeez, you're supposed to 
say something cheerful.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.960
All right, here we go.

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:47.770
Go, Kitauji!

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.410
Hey, that was my...

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:51.690
Wha?

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.650
<i>And so, with the Kansai Competition coming up,</i>

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.300
<i>the Kitauji High School Concert 
Band was off to the races.</i>

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.360
I'm so moved.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.910
You sure were practicing a lot.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.330
Could you hear me?

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.790
So the Monaka members talked it over,

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.800
and decided that we'd do 
everything we could.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.760
Reina?

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.760
Kousaka-san...

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.610
I thought you biked to school.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.180
Yeah.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.560
Moms' volleyball?

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.550
Yeah.

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:30.620
She wanted to borrow my bike to 
get to Taiyou Park every day.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:32.020
Taiyou Park?

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.900
That place is all uphill.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.990
I told her she should buy 
a bike with pedal assist.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:39.300
What a powerful mom.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.930
Then, does that mean we can walk 
home together for a while?

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:46.330
I'll be staying behind for sectionals, though.

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:48.190
We'll wait! Right?

00:10:48.190 --> 00:10:51.960
Sure, we're always waiting for 
people at the end of practice.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:54.710
I guess it's okay, then.

00:10:55.070 --> 00:10:56.850
Good!

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:59.150
I've been thinking

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:04.640
the first-years should stick together, 
not only with our sections.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.290
We talked about that in Monaka, too.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.810
Right?

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:11.050
<b>Train Arriving</b>

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:13.980
Okay, let's start tomorrow.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.130
If you have time, let's go for sweets.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.440
See you.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.630
Judging by the schedule sheet, 
I can't imagine we will.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.910
Don't say that.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.000
You start practice at six in the morning?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.740
Yeah.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:32.880
So early!

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:35.250
Bye.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:47.850
I thought you might not like going 
home with other people.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:49.810
Why not?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:54.230
Well, you said something like that before.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:02.290
I don't like hanging out with those 
that I have no interest in.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:05.660
But I don't hate either 
Kawashima-san or Katou-san.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:07.850
Really?

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:09.940
Yeah, why?

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.120
Nothing.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:16.590
<i>That's when I noticed that Reina 
had changed, just a little.</i>

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:22.970
<i>Through the audition, she'd discovered 
Kaori-senpai and Yuko-senpai's feelings.</i>

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:29.350
<i>Maybe she's trying to figure 
out what it means to strive</i>

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:32.610
<i>to be strong and special despite that.</i>

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.450
Winter uniforms are so stuffy.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.500
Yeah.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.560
See you tomorrow.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:39.520
Kumiko.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:41.940
Let's make it to the Nationals.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.290
Promise.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:45.610
Yeah.

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.300
Nationals, huh?

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.880
I'm home.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.330
Welcome home.

00:13:00.330 --> 00:13:02.400
Congratulations on winning the gold.

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:03.330
Yeah.

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:04.880
Dinner's ready.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:05.890
Okay.

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:08.890
I called Dad. He was really happy.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:10.850
Yeah?

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:14.050
Your sister wouldn't pick up the phone,

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:16.010
but I'm sure she'll be happy, too.

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.310
I wonder...

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:19.780
Of course,

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:22.300
she used to play music, too.

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:22.740
<b>Euphonium Technique 
Fun with the Euphonium 
High School Entrance Exam Questions 
Middle School Science Experiment Resources 
World of Ensembles 
Middle School English Dictionary 
Geographical Dictionary 
Language Questions 
Mathematics Questions 
High School Entrance Exam Strategy
History Vocabulary</b>

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.070
I doubt she cares anymore.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:34.410
<i>Here we are, a performance by the 
Seira Girls' High School Concert Band.</i>

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.560
This school's really good, right?

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:46.180
Yeah, they win first place 
at Nationals all the time.

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:50.430
And that's the school you're up against, huh?

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.100
If we make it to the Nationals, that is.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.430
You still have bed head.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.060
Are you sure you can practice that way?

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:43.700
I think so.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:46.240
I'm finally waking up.

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:47.860
Where are you going?

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.700
The staff office.

00:14:50.820 --> 00:14:52.770
I need the music room key.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.350
To open it.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.250
Good morning.

00:14:59.010 --> 00:14:59.940
Excuse us.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.210
Excuse us!

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:04.340
You're here, too, Oumae-san?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.100
Yes.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.970
Good for you, coming so early.

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:09.430
Um, may we have the music room key?

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:13.150
Yoroizuka-san took it earlier.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.390
It should already be open.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:17.090
Yoroizuka-san?

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:19.700
Mizore Yoroizuka-senpai, the oboist.

00:15:19.700 --> 00:15:21.740
She's always here before I am.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.480
Always?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.260
Thank you.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.570
Let me guess, you come early, 
so you can talk to Taki-sensei?

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.160
That's right.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:37.480
You're so adorable like that, Reina.

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:38.660
Don't give me that.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.290
I'm here to practice properly, too.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:57.500
It sounds good, but it's kind of dry...

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:06.010
Good morning.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.170
That's unusual.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.290
Two of you, today.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:31.500
Yes.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:32.970
There are two of us today.

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:35.470
I see.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:42.370
So, Yoroizuka-senpai, are you 
always here this early?

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:52.280
Yes, I am.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:54.450
You must like practicing.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.520
I don't know.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:05.210
<i>The oboe, whose voice is often 
compared to a beautiful, female voice.</i>

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:08.340
<i>It's difficult to tune,</i>

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:11.770
<i>and with an inside diameter of 4 
millimeters at its narrowest part,</i>

00:17:11.770 --> 00:17:14.300
<i>it demands strong breath-control technique.</i>

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.070
For that, it's earned a reputation of being 
the most difficult woodwind instrument.

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:24.560
But I didn't think she'd
be so unapproachable...

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.260
Really? I think she's fine.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:31.150
Yeah, I guess she resembles you in some ways.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.650
What is that supposed to mean?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.050
I didn't mean anything, really.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.070
Morning.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:38.410
Morning.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.490
Oumae's with you today?

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.120
It's okay... Sit back down and keep playing.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.370
Okay.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.670
Speaking of which,

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:57.310
I think Yoroizuka-senpai is close 
friends with Yuko-senpai.

00:17:57.310 --> 00:17:58.640
Yuko-senpai?

00:17:58.640 --> 00:17:59.610
Yeah.

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:01.040
They talk together a lot,

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.430
those two.

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:09.440
<i>Reina was right about that.</i>

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.440
Are you done with your summer 
break homework, Mizore?

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.150
About halfway.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.790
Lucky! I'm not even close.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.000
Hey, are you free for the Bon break?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.560
Want to work on it together?

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:21.490
Sure, I guess.

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.530
Yay!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:31.840
Yo.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.130
What are you looking at?

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:35.590
Nothing.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:37.970
Weird.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.340
Something doesn't feel right.

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:44.940
Hey.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:45.560
Yes?

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:49.440
Hey, you're a first-year brass, right?

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.590
Yes...

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:52.290
Is Asuka-senpai around?

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.450
Asuka-senpai?

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.940
Wait, Nozomi...

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.270
Who said you could go off by yourself?

00:18:57.270 --> 00:18:59.460
I told you we're waiting in Class 7.

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:01.100
But...

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.530
Natsuki-senpai?

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:10.080
If you try and pull something, you're the 
one who'll end up in trouble.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:11.790
Got it.

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:18.210
Thanks, Natsuki.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.310
You don't need to thank me.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.430
Oumae-chan, do me a favor,

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:31.290
and don't tell Asuka-senpai 
what you just saw.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:31.940
Huh?

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:33.650
Please.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.240
Sure, I guess.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.270
Thanks.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:42.290
What's up?

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.330
Nothing.

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:50.270
<i>That's what I said, but there was 
no way it wouldn't bother me.</i>

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:53.570
<i>Who was that again?</i>

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:56.900
<i>She came to watch the Kyoto 
Competition, didn't she?</i>

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:59.470
<i>And she wants to talk to Asuka-senpai?</i>

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:00.880
What?

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.720
<i>I could ask...</i>

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.730
But there's no way Asuka-senpai 
would tell me.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.030
You're talking out loud.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:08.100
Yikes.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:13.150
Please and thank you.

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.240
Please and thank you.

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.470
Please and thank you.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:21.160
All right, let's start the ensemble practice.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:24.240
But first, there's someone 
I'd like to introduce.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.950
No way, his fiancée?

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:29.830
Excuse me.

00:20:31.340 --> 00:20:35.290
He's a school graduate and a 
professional percussionist.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.170
He will be instructing you for the summer.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.080
A pro?

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:40.880
Seriously?

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.320
My name is Masahiro Hashimoto.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.090
Nice to meet you.

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.280
My nickname is "Hashimoto-chan."

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:50.180
Obviously, you can tell I went 
to college with Taki-kun.

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:55.150
Hit me up if there's anything you 
want to hear about Taki-kun.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:56.560
Oh?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.270
Tough crowd, huh?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.660
You can cut the chatter.

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:02.590
I bet Taki-kun's popular.

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:04.820
The girls must be all over him.

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:08.600
Yes.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.970
He's popular with the girls 
outside of Concert Band.

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.140
Not popular with concert band girls, huh?

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:16.520
Sorry about that.

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.080
Taki-kun's always had his foot in his mouth.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:19.670
Ow!

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.800
I told you to cut the chatter.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:30.490
Are you awake?

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.430
Y-Yes.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.720
You have a new coach, and you 
aren't even interested?

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:36.060
What a bummer.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:36.900
I'm sorry.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.820
Right, percussion!

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.590
Let's get started!

00:21:41.590 --> 00:21:42.400
Yes.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:46.320
<i>I have to concentrate.</i>

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.400
There's no time to breathe here.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:52.270
It's so tempting to rush.

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.000
Why not take a staggered breath?

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:56.710
Goto, when do you breathe?

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.080
Here.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.280
Oh, this rest...

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:02.300
You, too, Riko-chan?

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.640
Yes.

00:22:05.180 --> 00:22:09.290
Then, how about we have Goto 
breathe two bars after that?

00:22:09.290 --> 00:22:13.440
You don't have to try to get through 
this entire phrase, Riko-chan.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:14.600
Got it.

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:16.560
What about contrabass?

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:19.240
Sapphire Kawashima is perfect.

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:21.020
It's Midori.

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:25.490
Okay, with that in mind, let's try again.

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:25.490
Excuse me...

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:26.960
But first...

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.070
Kumiko Oumae!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:31.350
You aren't focused today.

00:22:31.350 --> 00:22:32.660
Is something wrong?

00:22:34.170 --> 00:22:36.130
You can talk to me about it.

00:22:36.130 --> 00:22:38.000
I won't bite.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:40.330
You do bite.

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.930
Just fess up!

00:22:41.930 --> 00:22:43.000
Ow, ow, ow...

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.090
Is something wrong, Kumiko-chan?

00:22:45.090 --> 00:22:46.470
Is there?

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:49.290
No, it's like...

00:22:49.290 --> 00:22:50.550
Asuka-senpai...

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:52.890
What's up?

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:55.850
I need to talk to you.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:57.410
What is it?

00:22:57.410 --> 00:22:58.420
Love?

00:22:58.420 --> 00:22:59.600
You want to talk about love?

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:00.730
No.

00:23:04.760 --> 00:23:06.970
We're in the middle of practice.

00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.280
At least hear me out.

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:12.870
Before I do, is it something you need 
to talk to me about personally?

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:15.330
Or to me as the vice president?

00:23:15.900 --> 00:23:17.290
Both.

00:23:17.740 --> 00:23:19.010
Fine.

00:23:19.480 --> 00:23:20.250
What?

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.090
Masami-chan...

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:38.100
I want to join the club again.

00:23:39.640 --> 00:23:40.560
Huh?

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:52.380
I hate competitions...

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:56.890
Mizore...

00:24:59.550 --> 00:25:02.270
Let's promise to get first place 
when we're in high school.

00:25:06.150 --> 00:25:07.000
Yeah.

00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:34.260
<b>Second Place, Minami Public Middle School</b>

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:37.370
You're kidding.

00:25:37.370 --> 00:25:39.260
This is just the Kyoto Competition.

00:25:40.370 --> 00:25:42.090
Minami Middle School got second.

00:25:42.640 --> 00:25:44.440
That doesn't happen often.

00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:46.650
Didn't they win the Kansai
Competition last year?

00:25:49.880 --> 00:25:51.000
Nozomi...

00:25:52.260 --> 00:25:53.590
Yeah?

00:25:53.590 --> 00:25:55.900
Were you serious about 
what you said earlier?

00:25:56.330 --> 00:25:57.530
What did I say earlier?

00:25:58.530 --> 00:26:00.350
About placing first in high school.

00:26:01.910 --> 00:26:02.750
Yeah.

00:26:03.280 --> 00:26:04.660
Let's win first place.

00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:16.800
I want to join the club again.

00:26:17.340 --> 00:26:19.800
Please let Nozomi back into the club.

00:26:22.570 --> 00:26:24.210
Oh, please.

00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:26.390
There's nothing I can do about it.

00:26:26.390 --> 00:26:28.520
I'm the vice president...

00:26:28.520 --> 00:26:30.560
I'm just a humble middle manager.

00:26:31.110 --> 00:26:32.540
Please!

00:26:32.540 --> 00:26:34.940
I want your approval, Asuka-senpai.

00:26:35.440 --> 00:26:36.770
Why?

00:26:36.770 --> 00:26:38.240
I've made up my mind.

00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:41.700
I won't rejoin unless I have your approval.

00:26:42.090 --> 00:26:45.580
That's nothing but troublesome for me.

00:26:45.920 --> 00:26:47.030
Please!

00:26:47.030 --> 00:26:48.830
Nozomi is serious.

00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:53.260
Sorry.

00:26:53.840 --> 00:26:56.760
Right now, we're in the middle of practice.

00:26:57.350 --> 00:26:58.760
Go away.

00:27:00.570 --> 00:27:03.830
I want the first-years to leave.

00:27:05.970 --> 00:27:07.700
We need to talk.

00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:14.530
This kind of sucks, with the 
first-years being left out.

00:27:14.870 --> 00:27:17.240
Remember this happened before, too?

00:27:21.690 --> 00:27:23.170
I wonder...

00:27:23.170 --> 00:27:26.350
Does it have something to do with 
the incident that made a lot

00:27:26.350 --> 00:27:28.160
of the second-years quit last year?

00:27:28.160 --> 00:27:31.210
You know, we're part of the club, too.

00:27:31.210 --> 00:27:33.760
Of course we want to know what's going on.

00:27:31.670 --> 00:27:35.420
<b>Congratulations 
Kansai Competition</b>

00:27:37.360 --> 00:27:40.590
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:27:41.340 --> 00:27:43.360
<i>And the day after that,</i>

00:27:43.360 --> 00:27:45.850
<i>Nozomi-senpai came to practice.</i>

00:27:46.290 --> 00:27:47.280
Sorry.

00:27:49.120 --> 00:27:53.640
It's summer break, and she's always here, 
waiting for practice to finish.

00:27:54.390 --> 00:27:58.180
Nozomi-senpai's <i>that</i> desperate to rejoin?

00:27:58.810 --> 00:28:01.570
Again, why not?

00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:05.610
Court is now adjourned.

00:28:05.610 --> 00:28:07.160
Let's get back to practice.

00:28:07.160 --> 00:28:08.640
Asuka-senpai...

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:12.170
Natsuki is friends with Nozomi-chan, so...

00:28:13.390 --> 00:28:18.550
Nozomi isn't trying to join the 
competition or anything.

00:28:19.110 --> 00:28:20.240
Exactly...

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:22.550
I just want to help.

00:28:22.550 --> 00:28:27.140
I told you, I don't have authority to decide.

00:28:27.540 --> 00:28:29.980
But I still want you to approve!

00:28:29.980 --> 00:28:32.020
Personally!

00:28:34.720 --> 00:28:35.960
Fine.

00:28:35.960 --> 00:28:37.520
I'll be honest with you, then.

00:28:38.120 --> 00:28:41.060
I don't agree with your rejoining.

00:28:41.060 --> 00:28:43.410
You wouldn't be an asset to the club.

00:28:43.760 --> 00:28:45.750
So stop coming by.

00:28:45.750 --> 00:28:46.810
Got it?

00:28:56.450 --> 00:28:58.250
What are you doing?

00:28:58.250 --> 00:28:59.460
President...

00:29:00.510 --> 00:29:03.000
Is Nozomi-chan here again?

00:29:03.470 --> 00:29:04.970
You knew?

00:29:05.460 --> 00:29:07.890
Asuka told me.

00:29:07.890 --> 00:29:10.130
What's going on?

00:29:10.130 --> 00:29:13.290
Oh, well, stuff.

00:29:13.290 --> 00:29:16.650
First-years don't need to worry about it. 
Just focus on practice.

00:29:17.550 --> 00:29:21.740
When you say it like that, I can't focus.

00:29:21.740 --> 00:29:24.610
I get that, but...

00:29:26.530 --> 00:29:29.760
No, you aren't getting anything out of me.

00:29:29.760 --> 00:29:31.470
Come on.

00:29:31.470 --> 00:29:34.600
But you know how a lot of 
members quit last year?

00:29:34.600 --> 00:29:35.420
Yes.

00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:38.920
Most of them were from 
Minami Middle School.

00:29:38.920 --> 00:29:40.380
Minami Middle School?

00:29:41.710 --> 00:29:44.550
Nozomi-chan and Natsuki-chan 
are from Minami, too.

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:47.380
I think that's why things are so complicated.

00:29:49.820 --> 00:29:51.560
Minami, huh?

00:29:52.020 --> 00:29:55.540
I think they won first place in the 
middle school division this year, too.

00:29:55.540 --> 00:29:57.410
Albeit a dud gold.

00:29:57.410 --> 00:30:00.570
But they got second place when we 
were in middle school, didn't they?

00:30:01.150 --> 00:30:05.720
I remember it was a pretty big deal 
that Minami only won second.

00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:09.070
But Natsuki-senpai wasn't in 
the concert band, was she?

00:30:09.070 --> 00:30:10.770
Apparently not.

00:30:10.770 --> 00:30:13.580
But I think she was close to Nozomi-senpai.

00:30:14.580 --> 00:30:18.960
I heard Yuko-senpai and Yoroizuka-senpai 
are both from Minami.

00:30:19.330 --> 00:30:20.710
Are they?

00:30:21.080 --> 00:30:22.880
Oh, so that's why.

00:30:26.360 --> 00:30:29.140
Watching Goto-senpai and Riko-senpai,

00:30:29.140 --> 00:30:35.560
I get the sense that what happened 
last year really left a mark on them.

00:30:35.560 --> 00:30:39.040
The second years, especially... 
They don't want to talk about it.

00:30:39.040 --> 00:30:42.230
They get really guarded when 
that topic comes up.

00:30:42.650 --> 00:30:44.420
I guess...

00:30:44.420 --> 00:30:47.960
Nearly half the grade dropped 
out at the same time.

00:30:47.960 --> 00:30:49.490
I'm sure they were shocked.

00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:55.910
I wonder if it's really that annoying that 
they'd want to come back now.

00:30:56.430 --> 00:30:57.670
I wonder...

00:30:57.670 --> 00:31:01.380
But that's what Asuka-senpai thinks, right?

00:31:01.380 --> 00:31:04.130
I feel like that's not the whole story.

00:31:07.490 --> 00:31:09.480
Three-second rule!

00:31:09.480 --> 00:31:11.640
I don't think you should do that...

00:31:13.640 --> 00:31:17.480
<b>Ujigawa Fireworks Festival</b>

00:31:14.750 --> 00:31:17.480
Oh, yeah, tomorrow's the fireworks festival.

00:31:18.260 --> 00:31:19.900
Are you two going?

00:31:19.900 --> 00:31:21.870
Actually, I can see it from my place.

00:31:21.870 --> 00:31:22.810
It's a bit far, though.

00:31:23.970 --> 00:31:25.400
What about you, Hazuki-chan?

00:31:25.400 --> 00:31:28.370
I think I'm going with my family.

00:31:28.370 --> 00:31:29.970
Midori said she's doing that, too.

00:31:30.860 --> 00:31:32.170
What about you, Kousaka-san?

00:31:32.170 --> 00:31:33.640
I haven't decided yet.

00:31:33.640 --> 00:31:34.720
Yeah?

00:31:37.690 --> 00:31:38.500
See you.

00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:39.750
Yeah.

00:31:43.420 --> 00:31:45.250
So, aren't you going?

00:31:45.650 --> 00:31:46.650
Going where?

00:31:46.650 --> 00:31:47.700
To the fireworks.

00:31:48.700 --> 00:31:51.090
I don't care either way.

00:31:51.690 --> 00:31:53.630
Want to go together, then?

00:31:54.540 --> 00:31:55.600
Huh?

00:31:58.270 --> 00:32:00.440
Wait, are you being shy?

00:32:00.440 --> 00:32:03.150
That isn't really it...

00:32:04.140 --> 00:32:07.290
I'm just not used to inviting people.

00:32:07.290 --> 00:32:10.010
But you invited me, huh?

00:32:10.010 --> 00:32:11.730
Stop grinning.

00:32:11.730 --> 00:32:13.150
I'm not.

00:32:13.150 --> 00:32:15.780
Are we going or not?

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:17.790
I'm home.

00:32:17.790 --> 00:32:19.730
Do you know where my yukata is?

00:32:19.730 --> 00:32:21.240
You're wearing it?

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:22.370
Yeah.

00:32:27.060 --> 00:32:27.920
Urgh.

00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:29.900
What do you mean, "Urgh"?

00:32:29.900 --> 00:32:31.030
You're home.

00:32:31.030 --> 00:32:33.320
At least knock.

00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:34.930
What are you even doing?

00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:37.000
I'm looking for my yukata.

00:32:39.500 --> 00:32:42.190
Hey, so you're going to the 
Kansai Competition?

00:32:43.680 --> 00:32:44.690
Yeah.

00:32:48.270 --> 00:32:49.320
Congrats.

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:50.750
Ow!

00:32:50.750 --> 00:32:52.440
What was that for?

00:32:59.320 --> 00:33:02.020
You really aren't a morning person, are you?

00:33:02.020 --> 00:33:03.290
Still not used to it?

00:33:04.070 --> 00:33:05.680
It's taking time.

00:33:07.740 --> 00:33:09.130
Good morning.

00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:19.310
Isn't that Myoujou Technical School?

00:33:19.310 --> 00:33:20.140
Yeah.

00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:26.650
Taki-sensei didn't notice you, huh?

00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:30.150
I think he's in deep thought about

00:33:30.150 --> 00:33:32.150
what we need to work on and stuff.

00:33:32.830 --> 00:33:36.660
We have to be able to compete 
with Myoujou Technical.

00:33:36.660 --> 00:33:38.630
Myoujou, huh?

00:33:38.630 --> 00:33:40.710
Aren't they a seed this year, too?

00:33:40.710 --> 00:33:41.520
Yeah.

00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:44.160
These past few years, they've been 
at all the Nationals.

00:33:45.250 --> 00:33:46.670
You haven't heard?

00:33:47.120 --> 00:33:48.670
What about?

00:33:48.670 --> 00:33:49.920
Oh...

00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:52.620
What should I do?

00:33:55.150 --> 00:33:57.850
Huh? You're both here early.

00:33:57.850 --> 00:33:59.500
Good morning.

00:33:59.500 --> 00:34:01.280
Morning.

00:34:09.270 --> 00:34:10.290
Yuko...

00:34:10.290 --> 00:34:11.280
Hmm?

00:34:12.100 --> 00:34:14.740
Are you not close with those two?

00:34:20.990 --> 00:34:23.310
Um...

00:34:24.200 --> 00:34:26.580
Are you, Senpai?

00:34:26.580 --> 00:34:30.460
Jeez, I don't know, underclassman.

00:34:33.940 --> 00:34:35.540
Um...

00:34:35.540 --> 00:34:40.970
We aren't close, and we aren't far. 
We're normal.

00:34:40.970 --> 00:34:41.930
Yeah.

00:34:41.930 --> 00:34:42.930
Normal.

00:34:42.930 --> 00:34:45.820
We're, like, senpai and junior.

00:34:45.820 --> 00:34:46.980
Probably.

00:34:49.280 --> 00:34:52.750
Okay, we're going to go practice outside.

00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:53.570
Let's go.

00:34:53.570 --> 00:34:55.620
After all that's happened?

00:34:55.620 --> 00:34:59.320
You sure are oblivious to club drama, Mizore.

00:35:00.190 --> 00:35:01.830
I'm not even interested.

00:35:02.220 --> 00:35:05.640
That's what's good about you, I guess.

00:35:09.050 --> 00:35:10.540
That thing from earlier...

00:35:10.540 --> 00:35:12.810
It's about Nozomi.

00:35:15.710 --> 00:35:16.840
Nozomi.

00:35:18.020 --> 00:35:18.980
Yeah.

00:35:18.980 --> 00:35:22.550
Apparently, Nozomi said she wants 
to come back to the band.

00:35:23.830 --> 00:35:24.870
I see.

00:35:41.540 --> 00:35:42.450
Okay.

00:35:42.450 --> 00:35:45.140
I'm bothered by the entry of 
the trumpets at the start.

00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:47.520
Don't come in with a "blah."

00:35:47.520 --> 00:35:50.790
Start it off with a bang.

00:35:50.790 --> 00:35:51.670
Yes.

00:35:52.140 --> 00:35:55.520
Also, the fortissimo sounds muddy.

00:35:56.000 --> 00:35:58.500
It has to be loud and beautiful.

00:35:58.500 --> 00:35:59.470
Yes.

00:36:00.930 --> 00:36:05.690
<i>I couldn't stop thinking 
about Yoroizuka-senpai's</i>

00:36:05.690 --> 00:36:08.510
<i>seemingly terrified face from the morning,</i>

00:36:08.510 --> 00:36:11.670
<i>especially since she always 
seemed so expressionless.</i>

00:36:11.670 --> 00:36:13.230
Yo, Knuckles.

00:36:13.500 --> 00:36:17.820
Can you tell percussion's roll at
the beginning is getting pretty accurate?

00:36:18.410 --> 00:36:22.530
It sounded fine when we started, 
but it was kind of rough.

00:36:22.800 --> 00:36:23.930
Yes.

00:36:23.930 --> 00:36:26.790
Taki-sensei pointed it out several times,

00:36:26.790 --> 00:36:28.710
but I feel I've finally gotten the hang of it.

00:36:28.710 --> 00:36:30.380
I know, right?

00:36:30.380 --> 00:36:33.420
You can go ahead and respect 
me even more.

00:36:34.810 --> 00:36:36.760
Is there anything else?

00:36:37.200 --> 00:36:38.530
Let's see...

00:36:39.040 --> 00:36:42.430
Overall, you seem pretty reserved and quiet.

00:36:42.880 --> 00:36:46.560
It's like your personalities are 
showing in the way you play.

00:36:46.560 --> 00:36:50.010
You should all be more imposing.

00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:53.690
Like, if there's something on 
your mind, just say it.

00:36:54.280 --> 00:36:55.240
Got it?

00:36:55.240 --> 00:36:56.430
Yes.

00:36:56.430 --> 00:36:59.400
Okay, let's take it from the same spot again.

00:37:00.840 --> 00:37:03.990
I thought that he was just
kind of funny, but...

00:37:04.590 --> 00:37:07.870
Hashimoto-sensei sure is a pro.

00:37:07.870 --> 00:37:11.130
I think it's a good idea for 
each section to comment

00:37:11.130 --> 00:37:12.960
on the other sections, too.

00:37:12.960 --> 00:37:14.560
That's true.

00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:16.900
We didn't really do that 
kind of thing before.

00:37:16.900 --> 00:37:18.620
What can you expect?

00:37:18.620 --> 00:37:22.930
People have been kind of sensitive, 
especially with what happened last year.

00:37:24.140 --> 00:37:25.390
Thanks.

00:37:25.390 --> 00:37:29.210
We can't keep worrying about that forever.

00:37:29.210 --> 00:37:30.640
Start fresh and go!

00:37:33.340 --> 00:37:35.100
I forgot my water bottle.

00:37:35.100 --> 00:37:36.800
Is it in the music room?

00:37:36.800 --> 00:37:38.460
It might be in the hallway.

00:37:38.460 --> 00:37:39.710
I'll catch up.

00:37:50.540 --> 00:37:52.160
Yoroizuka-senpai?

00:37:52.640 --> 00:37:54.320
What's wrong?

00:37:54.320 --> 00:37:55.580
Are you okay?

00:37:56.190 --> 00:37:57.670
I feel sick.

00:37:57.670 --> 00:37:59.730
Want to go to the nurse's office?

00:37:59.730 --> 00:38:01.860
Though, I don't know if it's still open.

00:38:01.860 --> 00:38:03.590
No, it's fine.

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:06.380
But you look pale.

00:38:07.830 --> 00:38:09.380
Don't mind me.

00:38:18.350 --> 00:38:19.570
<i>This sound...</i>

00:38:22.080 --> 00:38:24.610
<i>It's the flutist from Minami Middle School.</i>

00:38:26.660 --> 00:38:27.990
I'm going to vomit.

00:38:28.510 --> 00:38:30.030
You should take it easy.

00:38:30.620 --> 00:38:33.040
I don't want to hear this sound.

00:38:39.200 --> 00:38:41.500
It's the euphonium girl.

00:38:41.880 --> 00:38:43.840
Senpai, is that—

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:47.410
Oh, don't worry, it's mine.

00:38:47.410 --> 00:38:50.020
I wanted to play it a little, so I brought it.

00:38:50.830 --> 00:38:52.940
Aren't you early, though?

00:38:52.940 --> 00:38:56.230
Since the fireworks festival is starting, 
we're done for the day.

00:38:57.390 --> 00:38:59.360
Then Asuka-senpai's already...

00:38:59.690 --> 00:39:01.370
Yes, I think so.

00:39:01.370 --> 00:39:02.610
Oh.

00:39:04.410 --> 00:39:06.530
You're good on the flute.

00:39:06.930 --> 00:39:08.180
Thanks.

00:39:08.180 --> 00:39:10.620
At Minami, they wouldn't let us play flute,

00:39:10.620 --> 00:39:12.910
unless we had our own instruments.

00:39:12.910 --> 00:39:15.000
I begged my parents to buy me one.

00:39:16.370 --> 00:39:18.490
You must really like flute.

00:39:21.250 --> 00:39:22.840
I do.

00:39:22.840 --> 00:39:23.980
I love it.

00:39:28.470 --> 00:39:29.760
It's so tight.

00:39:30.380 --> 00:39:32.600
It looks better tighter.

00:39:32.600 --> 00:39:35.270
I won't be able to eat much.

00:39:35.270 --> 00:39:37.600
Have you gained weight again?

00:39:37.600 --> 00:39:39.310
How could you say that?

00:39:39.730 --> 00:39:41.780
Don't get it dirty.

00:39:41.780 --> 00:39:42.790
Fine, fine.

00:39:44.230 --> 00:39:46.580
Did Onee-chan go home already?

00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:47.970
Who knows?

00:39:47.970 --> 00:39:51.300
These days, that girl's such a drifter.

00:40:00.110 --> 00:40:01.330
Hot...

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:05.710
Yukatas aren't as airy as they say.

00:40:09.540 --> 00:40:11.270
Sorry, I'm kind of late.

00:40:12.510 --> 00:40:14.100
Ten minutes late.

00:40:15.750 --> 00:40:16.670
Wow.

00:40:17.440 --> 00:40:18.980
You're super pretty.

00:40:20.790 --> 00:40:21.980
Yeah?

00:40:23.080 --> 00:40:24.020
What?

00:40:24.020 --> 00:40:27.990
I feel a bit intimidated, walking next to you.

00:40:27.990 --> 00:40:29.270
Why?

00:40:29.710 --> 00:40:30.740
Let's go.

00:40:35.780 --> 00:40:37.540
So many people...

00:40:38.580 --> 00:40:42.920
<b>Buttered Potatoes                    Takoyaki</b>

00:40:39.100 --> 00:40:40.950
I want shaved ice.

00:40:40.950 --> 00:40:41.960
Blue Hawaii.

00:40:41.960 --> 00:40:42.920
What about you?

00:40:42.920 --> 00:40:45.680
Croissant taiyaki... and samosas.

00:40:45.680 --> 00:40:46.620
Say what?

00:40:46.620 --> 00:40:47.920
They have that?

00:40:47.920 --> 00:40:55.680
<b>Frankfurters</b>

00:40:48.560 --> 00:40:50.830
Okay, I'm going to go buy shaved ice.

00:40:50.830 --> 00:40:52.440
And you're getting that taiyaki.

00:40:52.990 --> 00:40:54.570
I want strawberry.

00:40:54.570 --> 00:40:55.680
Got it.

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:59.070
Then again, do they have any around here?

00:41:00.180 --> 00:41:01.300
Oh.

00:41:01.300 --> 00:41:03.060
Hey, you're here.

00:41:03.460 --> 00:41:04.440
I'm here.

00:41:05.350 --> 00:41:06.800
Yakisoba, huh?

00:41:06.800 --> 00:41:07.970
Yeah, so?

00:41:07.970 --> 00:41:09.440
Yakisoba's good.

00:41:11.040 --> 00:41:12.570
The Agata Festival...

00:41:12.570 --> 00:41:13.950
Do you want to go with me?

00:41:13.950 --> 00:41:16.750
If you want, I wouldn't mind coming with you.

00:41:16.750 --> 00:41:17.370
Ack!

00:41:17.830 --> 00:41:19.370
Kousaka's with you, too?

00:41:19.830 --> 00:41:20.850
Well?

00:41:21.560 --> 00:41:23.870
Not really. We don't have to.

00:41:24.230 --> 00:41:25.230
Let's go.

00:41:26.140 --> 00:41:27.260
Later.

00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:34.200
I think spineless guys aren't any good.

00:41:34.200 --> 00:41:35.120
Hmm?

00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:37.140
Yeah, I guess.

00:41:38.150 --> 00:41:39.640
So indifferent.

00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:40.590
Hmm?

00:41:41.170 --> 00:41:42.640
Here, strawberry.

00:41:42.640 --> 00:41:45.020
Class 3 rapid fire.

00:41:45.410 --> 00:41:47.540
Opening: Starmine.

00:41:48.120 --> 00:41:53.640
<i>The Tale of Genji</i> is reborn, 
one thousand years later.

00:42:02.460 --> 00:42:03.910
It's so pretty.

00:42:04.590 --> 00:42:08.670
It's been a while since I stopped 
to watch fireworks.

00:42:09.080 --> 00:42:11.180
Last year, we were busy with exam prep.

00:42:14.210 --> 00:42:16.090
That's what you get for scarfing it down.

00:42:17.970 --> 00:42:19.470
Three-second rule!

00:42:20.530 --> 00:42:22.850
I'm not eating it.

00:42:23.590 --> 00:42:26.900
Oh, yeah. I did this with my 
sister when I was a kid.

00:42:29.820 --> 00:42:34.390
Hey, Reina, you've always lived 
for the trumpet, right?

00:42:34.390 --> 00:42:35.320
Yeah.

00:42:35.910 --> 00:42:37.520
Do you like the trumpet?

00:42:37.520 --> 00:42:39.340
Yeah, I do.

00:42:39.340 --> 00:42:40.370
Why?

00:42:41.120 --> 00:42:44.930
Today, I saw Nozomi-senpai 
playing the flute.

00:42:44.930 --> 00:42:46.260
After practice?

00:42:46.260 --> 00:42:47.290
Yeah.

00:42:47.290 --> 00:42:50.380
I talked to her, and she said she loves flute.

00:42:53.380 --> 00:42:56.880
I wonder why Asuka-senpai won't 
give her approval to rejoin.

00:42:56.880 --> 00:42:58.780
Because she doesn't want to.

00:42:59.340 --> 00:43:02.580
If she lets her in and Nozomi-senpai 
thrashes around,

00:43:02.580 --> 00:43:04.910
it would affect the Kansai Competition.

00:43:05.510 --> 00:43:08.400
I think Asuka-senpai is making 
the right decision.

00:43:08.400 --> 00:43:11.900
Doesn't not being able to 
play with everyone suck,

00:43:11.900 --> 00:43:14.310
even though you like playing?

00:43:14.310 --> 00:43:16.400
It's her fault for quitting.

00:43:17.140 --> 00:43:19.820
She knew that was what would happen.

00:43:19.820 --> 00:43:21.780
I know, but...

00:43:23.800 --> 00:43:26.790
I think quitting is running away.

00:43:27.280 --> 00:43:30.880
I don't know if she's running from 
upperclassmen she hates,

00:43:30.880 --> 00:43:33.580
from her classmates, or from herself.

00:43:34.080 --> 00:43:35.300
But she ran away.

00:43:38.730 --> 00:43:40.800
I would never run away.

00:43:41.310 --> 00:43:43.310
If I didn't like them, I'd beat them down.

00:43:43.960 --> 00:43:46.330
She quit, even though she couldn't do that.

00:43:46.330 --> 00:43:48.060
So she ran away.

00:43:48.750 --> 00:43:50.190
That's so like you.

00:43:50.570 --> 00:43:51.670
Is it?

00:43:51.670 --> 00:43:52.930
It's normal.

00:43:53.840 --> 00:43:56.400
We're aiming for the Nationals.

00:43:56.800 --> 00:43:59.450
We're trying to become special.

00:44:00.520 --> 00:44:03.770
If we make it to the Nationals, 
will we be special?

00:44:04.370 --> 00:44:05.490
I don't know.

00:44:05.490 --> 00:44:09.280
But if we can't even do that, 
we can't become special.

00:44:10.530 --> 00:44:11.980
I guess.

00:44:17.690 --> 00:44:19.820
I'm glad we came together.

00:44:19.820 --> 00:44:20.800
Yeah.

00:44:21.310 --> 00:44:23.510
Next year, let's come again.

00:44:23.900 --> 00:44:24.840
Really?

00:44:25.380 --> 00:44:26.490
Why?

00:44:26.490 --> 00:44:27.700
Nothing.

00:44:27.140 --> 00:44:29.100
The wait is over.

00:44:29.100 --> 00:44:31.560
The finale has begun.

00:44:32.030 --> 00:44:36.510
Enjoy the world of the Heian picture scrolls.

00:44:37.730 --> 00:44:40.110
Class 5 rapid fire.

00:44:40.110 --> 00:44:41.280
Starmine.

00:44:42.340 --> 00:44:46.380
The romance of Hikaru Genji, eternal.

00:45:06.340 --> 00:45:09.060
<i>This time isn't eternal.</i>

00:45:09.830 --> 00:45:13.400
<i>Someday, I'll part with the friends I love.</i>

00:45:13.820 --> 00:45:16.560
<i>No matter how hard I wish otherwise, 
in the blink of an eye,</i>

00:45:16.560 --> 00:45:18.130
<i>everything becomes part of the past.</i>

00:45:21.990 --> 00:45:27.140
<i>If only I could stuff this moment in time 
into a container to store it on ice.</i>

00:45:29.080 --> 00:45:33.030
<i>That way, I wouldn't have anything 
to be worried about.</i>

00:45:34.070 --> 00:45:35.250
What's wrong?

00:46:03.460 --> 00:46:07.460
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>
